  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigating Human-Jaguar Conflict, Facilitating Stakeholder Cooperation and Capacity, and Increasing Sustainable Use of Native Habitat in the Gran Chaco</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funds under this award are to reduce the mortality of jaguars, and increase jaguar habitat, in the Gran Chaco of Paraguay, Bolivia, and Argentina. Our specific activities include: (1) expanding our participatory network of private landowners and impact through the installation of new non-lethal, solar-powered electric conflict deterrent fences; (2) inventories and mapping of current and prospective participatory stakeholder properties to incentivize the establishment of legal private reserves and evaluate potential to restore habitat; (3) hosting the first series of human-jaguar conflict mitigation workshops in cooperation with regional livestock associations and in the most affected rural areas (4) engaging local youth and communities through a series of presentations and discussions at rural schools, and (5) hosting and running the first consumer focus groups to develop and refine market strategies for a sustainable supply chain.</narrative>
  </description>
